**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryControlsTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SourceAndDetectorMoveTests`

**How to implement.** The UI suite's remaining seed readers, which bind or show a seeded sample, read the shipped catalogue instead (001 §B 'tests load the same files'; the S1.7 brief: re-point every test that reads a seed value to the BuiltinCatalogue fixture, numbers unchanged). Files, all in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/`: `AppContextTests.fs`, `ElementMenuTests.fs`, `ExperimentControlsTests.fs`, `LayerBandsControlsTests.fs`, `LibraryControlsTests.fs`, `SourceAndDetectorMoveTests.fs`, `WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs`, `WireUiCompositionTests.fs`. Re-point rules (S1.7; the same in every re-point step). `builtInEntries` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.materials ()`; `standardCategories` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.categories ()`; `MaterialLibrary.standard` (written `standard` under `open MaterialLibrary`) becomes `{ entries = BuiltinCatalogue.materials () }`; `SeedSamples.allSeedSamples` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.samples ()`; `SeedSamples.<name>` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sample SampleIds.<name>Id` and `SeedSamples.<name>.id` becomes `SampleIds.<name>Id` (step 15's names); `SeedSources.allSeedSources` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sources ()`; `SeedSources.reference600` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.source600`; the `SeedSources.tunables` list becomes `[ PresetIds.xenonMonochromator; PresetIds.tiSapphireTunable; PresetIds.supercontinuum; PresetIds.euvBeamline ] |> List.map BuiltinCatalogue.source`, and one tunable source becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.xenonMonochromator`; `seedEntries` becomes `(BuiltinCatalogue.samples () |> List.map SampleItem) @ BuiltinCatalogue.presets ()`; `Library.createInMemory ()` (written `createInMemory ()` under `open Library`) becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()`; and the self-seeding stores become the fixture's doubles with the same arguments (step 45): `MaterialProxy.createInMemory r v` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore r v`, `SampleProxy.createInMemory v` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sampleStore v` and `CategoryProxy.createInMemory r` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.categoryStore r`. A fact that took a seed by its list position (`List.head`, `List.item`) takes the same entry by its well-known id (`MaterialIds`, `CategoryIds`, `SampleIds`, `PresetIds`), so it still tests the entry it tested; a fact that compared ordered lists built from the seed lists builds both sides from the fixture, and compares order-independently only where the product's order is not the fixture's row order (the S1.3 step 20 precedent). Every fact keeps its name and its assertions, every count and every number stays. A comment or doc, an `open`'s trailing comment included, that names a seed or a self-seeding store names the fixture member instead, in no more words, and an `open` nothing needs any more goes. No product file, fixture member or fact is added. Each of these files names a seeded sample (`SeedSamples.<name>` or its `id`), which becomes its `SampleIds` member or `BuiltinCatalogue.sample`. After this step no constructor or UI test calls a self-seeding store, which step 58 relies on when it gives the empty stores the plain name.

**Acceptance.** After the re-point, `git grep -n -E "SeedSamples|SeedSources|seedEntries|seedTrees|builtInEntries|standardCategories|seedExperiments|(MaterialProxy|SampleProxy|CategoryProxy).createInMemory |Library.createInMemory " -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests` MUST find nothing, so neither test suite names a seed or calls a self-seeding store; ui-smoke MUST pass with its count unchanged; ui-tests MUST pass over the touched classes with their counts unchanged; and build, elevation and the seven s07 invariants MUST pass.
